  displayName: 
  <Tags>k__BackingField: 
  <Icon>k__BackingField: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 44f0b2c512093924f82fc83e489e9cac, type: 3}
  <AboutText>k__BackingField: '<b><size=+10>Overview</size></b>

    Golf Solitaire
    is the original game in the aptly named "Golf"

    - First appears in 1905 book
    "Games of Patience" written by "Tarbart"

    - Initially under the name "One
    Foundation"

    - Changed to "Golf" because people were keeping score based
    on how many cards remained at the end, with the goal to finish with the lowest
    number possible

    - Wrap around appeared later

    - King->Queen wasn''t
    always present

    - First digital version was "Solitaire Royale" in 1987 for
    DOS

    - While not as popular as variants like Klondike and Spider, it remains
    a common Solitaire variant

    - Precursor game to other popular games like
    Tri-Peaks and Black Hole

    <b><size=+10>History</size></b>

    <b><size=+10>Today</size></b>'
  <GuideObject>k__BackingField: {fileID: 6214578951917086794, guid: 630c4c1cb94f32943ab9dfa337c39652, type: 3}
